#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 840.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167904} :activity/id #uuid "70c56636-a16b-5974-b39b-c312a1a1e556" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049209 :topic/id #uuid "e362b30c-c362-5928-a478-dbcc78543cc7" :topic/math-academy-id 3241} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167904 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168009 :tutorial/content "In this topic, we'll study phase portraits of linear systems\n![](images/b0/b083c5707c4e9aed3141fe638c55a1ed2dc3ad6569f122bef307550c94fe6a8b.svg)\nwhere the eigenvalues of a ![](images/25/2521651122403a440e682fef383af333958f5b0d1334abe8b0771865d4daf100.svg) matrix ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) are\n![](images/ee/eee119e3e35f381a1d66d9e1e75b27d89e68d5f72307f4e792887d5d7e9d0099.svg)\n\nLet ![](images/37/37030865839993f96fced21145844e8fca9c6d44e7922c623fe8e0bef98ef154.svg) where ![](images/0d/0d26960845a9f13b07c87e80faa88162c1dda64123f13567958d00aaa0a4dc94.svg) be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue ![](images/fa/faa0f885195eacb91222dc9ccc18cf7ab891a17bd787359d13bf4e72bf09d703.svg)\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n![](images/c4/c44ac9f2de14beffd3411373047316c888a93815d2f90d338f500ca329f66355.svg)\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n![](images/e9/e90f20affdff00fd5fb24e5b6f75c31d42a0e5b2ad52b38b2d4456ee6555bfc8.svg)\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n![](images/62/6224eb38da8f189696cbda057a5568d71310d64574d36e80af6e1a11ceed6d6e.svg)\n\nNotice that ![](images/42/42bbe4d12055825e9c24b2dfc1a6ca306cb2675c13d039fbdb67e2170788c612.svg) and ![](images/ca/ca0400387ee619b6e2ddc7028859cf5902aecb715c38ec71e43b0f9056533cb6.svg) are bounded, so the factor ![](images/b0/b051bd1eb312485960edb54d28ffe85da63acab1c5f20b59466d01f55cba034c.svg) controls the long-term behavior:\n\n- If ![](images/0a/0a23a6577131711d405eb650b1d9d8429ca07d07bb9759644c407121643dcf5e.svg) then ![](images/9a/9a15a0d668c2a7ab9457f6a4c605858e03ddbb3ff93f3667d0deb0def1e206b1.svg) as ![](images/e5/e54727d514ed264e6dd30c7f4044746e6d2b4b462dc3776daecf7eb68634c358.svg) So, trajectories are *unbounded*, and we have a *spiral* that is traversed toward infinity as ![](images/e5/e54727d514ed264e6dd30c7f4044746e6d2b4b462dc3776daecf7eb68634c358.svg) In particular, the trajectory is unbounded for ![](images/bb/bb0d93faa0ccc44575fe83f9f7a644895ced86c18e9908a8e0d6dc6a36378d7d.svg)\n\n- If ![](images/28/28e6012b2b10c0a7f40681ab8a73666a12afd6e976c59f536ed30d1defca5f64.svg) then ![](images/2b/2b74153553b7dab9ad3a92e31ddd3b09ba44e4ba0e451229e924f227087fb58b.svg) as ![](images/e5/e54727d514ed264e6dd30c7f4044746e6d2b4b462dc3776daecf7eb68634c358.svg) So, trajectories *approach the origin*, and we have a *spiral* that is traversed toward the origin as ![](images/e5/e54727d514ed264e6dd30c7f4044746e6d2b4b462dc3776daecf7eb68634c358.svg) In particular, the trajectory is bounded for ![](images/23/23f355a7475101ff2d8f72842b5c291fcddc7b934d9e6a05c63b71c50443a334.svg) although it is unbounded if ![](images/70/707bb132def3690d81bf1f0c8cf416c1382322ab19d66264cdab1decc4669307.svg) is allowed to approach ![](images/8e/8ef8c99c128deb7895aefe6d1a662021e675d3609017391dd57526f775a30207.svg)\n\n- If ![](images/ba/ba33162d712db6f36bcf09e725d626c399881e98edb06cdc4ddfd17532b06701.svg) then ![](images/88/88318ea5b5d7fde77eace946e939b02b531330ff006ea20c887ea2f654acbdf9.svg) for all ![](images/a9/a90dc11635a0cfd7e959687183800180490f43955de346f70950a5720cd92df4.svg) So, trajectories are *bounded*, and we have an *ellipse*.\n\nLet's see some concrete examples." :tutorial/id #uuid "2a925aab-4f30-57a3-a3a2-6c3e21b5b318" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14482 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "7b0e4834-5b7b-5ae6-a7c1-b1def5543b1d" :step/math-academy-id 594290 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167905}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167905 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168010 :tutorial/content "Consider the system of linear differential equations below.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}x(t)-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=4x(t)+\\frac{1}{2}y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda_{1,2} = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\pm4\\text{i},$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are $\\mathbf{v}_{1,2} = [\\pm \\text{i}, 1]^T,$ respectively. Given that the general solution of the system is\n![](images/d1/d13abb97b171049a17544fcb312b71d2da3d9294788c1aebe7aa969e99b7819c.svg)\nwe are interested in sketching the phase portrait of the system of differential equations given above.\n\nIf we set $c_1 = 1$ and $c_2 = 0$ in the general solution of the system, we obtain the particular solution:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x={e}^{t/2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ y={e}^{t/2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $\\dfrac{\\pi}{16}$ | $\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0.78$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $0.78$ | $1.22$ |\n\nLet's sketch this solution in the phase space.\n\n![](images/4f/4f9da4b66977b98b983477d22abb6e00135ea0e1bfa9f785cd0a62d674a7b782.png)\n\nNotice that $|\\sin(4t)| \\leq 1$ and $|\\cos(4t)| \\leq 1,$ but $e^{t/2} \\to \\infty$ as $t \\to \\infty.$ Thus, the obtained curve is unbounded. So, we have a spiral that is traversed counterclockwise.\n\nAgain, since $e^{t/2} \\to \\infty$ as $t \\to \\infty,$ the spiral is traversed toward infinity as $t \\to \\infty.$\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/62/62380812d6fbe4e28531a455814296a4969a0744fb28a94a5e2d7c588ec5cfc4.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "f3d4213d-a0e4-5bda-9e29-8eca4801de63" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14483 :tutorial/title "Systems With Complex Eigenvalues"} :step/id #uuid "89ecb234-3886-5849-970a-abafcfaa1df5" :step/math-academy-id 594291 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167906}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167906 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166941 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166550 :question/id #uuid "8337af7a-73e8-5ae2-9bed-b03f193b2950" :question/math-academy-id "e-21657"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "113b981d-bbf2-588a-be74-028506cdb19d" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048395} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048992} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049672} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050309}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167223} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167224} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308498} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308501} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427137} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427141} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534012}] :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Phase Portrait of a System"} :step/id #uuid "94fe1e57-9c9a-561e-bfd5-2ae1e6a4369a" :step/math-academy-id 594292 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167907}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167907 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166942 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166551 :question/id #uuid "7b4f569b-ad3a-5a93-a53e-27a186b7700e" :question/math-academy-id "e-21658"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b542bd66-f4f8-5b4e-a3e7-4717827c427a" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048535}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167229} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167242} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308591} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308592} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385185} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391460} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427136} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427140} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427143} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523972} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524032}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parameters of a System Given Its Phase Portrait"} :step/id #uuid "6468cc1a-a1a6-502b-82f1-16821ba5d8c4" :step/math-academy-id 594295 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167908}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167908 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168025 :tutorial/content "Finally, let’s summarize what we’ve learned so far.\n\nAgain, we are considering a linear system\n![](images/65/6597a81f818926afff9056180de0e12357ef7631be093aba32626a7461079c18.svg)\nwhere the eigenvalues of a $2 \\times 2$ matrix $A$ are\n\n$$\n\\lambda_{1,2}=a\\pm bi,\n\\qquad b\\neq 0.\n$$\n\nAs for the classification of the equilibrium at the origin, we get the following:\n\n- The type of the curve is determined by the parameter $a{:}$\n\n- If $a=0,$ we have bounded closed curves (ellipses/circles).\n\n- If $a \\neq 0,$ we have spirals.\n\n- The stability is determined by the sign of $a{:}$\n\n- If $a>0,$ we have an **unstable spiral** (source).\n\n- If $a<0,$ we have a **stable spiral** (sink).\n\n- If $a=0,$ we have a **center**.\n\n**Note:** The center is a *stable* equilibrium but not *asymptotically stable* since trajectories do not converge to it.\n\nLet's see an example." :tutorial/id #uuid "c36d256f-edd3-5079-9f72-da6e3a8b4f91" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14575 :tutorial/title "Classification of Equilibria"} :step/id #uuid "6209ec28-abe9-501f-8925-5c8a06aee7df" :step/math-academy-id 594299 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167909}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167909 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166943 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166552 :question/id #uuid "d7b40689-7b7e-546e-9b66-30e6a95f3ee0" :question/math-academy-id "e-21659"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f0b176c-c802-5b3b-85d0-dede602c9bf3" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048990}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167230} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167243} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308593} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308594} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308595} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308596} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308597} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308598} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427138} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427139} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427142} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534066}] :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Systems of Linear Differential Equations With Complex Eigenvalues"} :step/id #uuid "4d18ae8d-2ebf-569f-bebb-2a856d39ef9d" :step/math-academy-id 594300}] :activity/title "Phase Portraits for Linear Systems With Complex Eigenvalues" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186167012}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046644} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524083} :activity/id #uuid "f52aa899-b1e0-52c3-865d-5560a2dc7dfa" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049209 :topic/id #uuid "e362b30c-c362-5928-a478-dbcc78543cc7" :topic/math-academy-id 3241} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524053 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523972 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8b75148-d95a-5d08-af11-4aa07ce8700e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523673} {:answer/id #uuid "dc98cdc5-c359-530d-af31-67e1bfb44e23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "infinity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523714}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523673} :answer-field/id #uuid "9421f7fa-1c8e-53be-a123-4c39ce614322" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523867} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0a30d5b-c52b-5d64-9e7a-685ee21f652e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "unbounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523589} {:answer/id #uuid "c49d575e-35e3-5a93-a205-d45ca07df6e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "bounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523667}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523589} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a05d8e3-5b15-538e-8600-72f7c77a4c2b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523869} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75f5d8f1-f1cb-584a-8acd-7d759274decb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "counterclockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523494} {:answer/id #uuid "b499c7eb-c10e-535f-b1ac-b1a6bfe31a65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "clockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523634}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523494} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac708e0d-1927-567f-9585-04ae386c932f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523872} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b169055-907a-517e-8fb9-7101aeaf0308" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "an ellipse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523508} {:answer/id #uuid "98502b70-5818-5252-840c-915e2349bc46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "a spiral" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523572}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523572} :answer-field/id #uuid "af031759-1c5f-5644-acc3-f8e47567aef5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523876} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "439226bb-a6a9-5bb8-a8e7-a50c3987bc49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523392} {:answer/id #uuid "ddc10df4-39dd-583d-baa4-d277ab1be472" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523718}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523718} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9cb65c4-4123-5279-9ed5-4cc0602834eb" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523908} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2723674-043c-59b3-b271-31a43d927983" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523595} {:answer/id #uuid "a29ac787-f783-550b-a176-66b674d9200f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "b=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523597} {:answer/id #uuid "ff03cd61-bc7d-575e-9f61-f7fc9dab0ac8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a\\ne 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523786}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523786} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9ccf2e4-ade4-527a-9ccf-b085485fa9d7" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523916}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "78d32ec9-eea0-570e-81c9-743259524853" :question/math-academy-id "q-334286" :question/problem "![](images/1e/1e116b0a2ba3678cde3b321b23500f532037b0cafd3842be008ee8abc3c0ee28.png)\n\nThe phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two complex eigenvalues $\\lambda =a\\pm b\\text{i}$ is shown above. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe given curve is \n{{field-1}},\nrepresenting\n{{field-2}}\nthat is traversed \n{{field-3}}.\nThus, we must have \n{{field-4}}.\n\nThe spiral is traversed toward \n{{field-5}}\nas $t\\to \\infty .$\nHence, \n{{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow notice that the given curve is $\\text{unbounded},$ representing $\\text{a spiral}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$ Thus, we must have $a\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, notice that the spiral is traversed toward $\\text{the origin}.$\n\nHence, to insure that ${e}^{at}\\to 0,$ we require $a<0.$"} :step/id #uuid "3d934a50-1cd4-5216-bb35-6060f0b5e4e2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524084}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524083 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524032 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bd91dd1-c90f-56c1-8a22-a4fb47fa5f76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "an ellipse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523310} {:answer/id #uuid "e2128144-a4af-5256-b36a-5181f7ed5ef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "a spiral" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523726}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523310} :answer-field/id #uuid "083b0ba0-7609-5ec6-a938-3390e2910826" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523794} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f84dc65-c809-58fe-9248-5825204dea7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "bounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523415} {:answer/id #uuid "52d8604d-3b08-5dfc-b1df-7bfe0e66fe43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "unbounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523421}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523415} :answer-field/id #uuid "43cb95e9-51cf-599a-bd5e-a3c29f1f9c2d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523822} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35c949f2-67bb-5cc5-ab89-4f36613e0369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "clockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523367} {:answer/id #uuid "9b6e12f4-9d18-5592-b8ff-e4e7d21e2354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "counterclockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523