 solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow notice that the given curve is $\\text{unbounded},$ representing $\\text{a spiral}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$ Thus, we must have $a\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, notice that the spiral is traversed toward $\\text{infinity}.$\n\nHence, to insure that ${e}^{at}\\to \\infty ,$ we require $a>0.$"} :step/id #uuid "a015cce1-74cb-5e4f-9268-b88d722a4a5f"}] :activity/title "Phase Portraits for Linear Systems With Complex Eigenvalues" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523248}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549092} :activity/id #uuid "d990f3a7-db2b-51f0-8db9-f30c83207610" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049209 :topic/id #uuid "e362b30c-c362-5928-a478-dbcc78543cc7" :topic/math-academy-id 3241} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549082 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ab64725-1a4e-5e6f-b75b-c182cb4eecb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "infinity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385187} {:answer/id #uuid "a8539d93-6feb-5b04-ae8d-c2b02c265c8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385188}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385187} :answer-field/id #uuid "57f0b0eb-651f-550c-b679-4c2a64be72a6" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385186} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a841a040-ca8a-52f5-93b6-24780a6bca9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175