t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow notice that the given curve is $\\text{unbounded},$ representing $\\text{a spiral}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$ Thus, we must have $a\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, notice that the spiral is traversed toward $\\text{infinity}.$\n\nHence, to insure that ${e}^{at}\\to \\infty ,$ we require $a>0.$"} :step/id #uuid "17236c24-ba39-5f16-a290-16a88cca22fb"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549092 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167229 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bd46fd9-4ec6-5d4d-b935-c34269ce5266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548524} {:answer/id #uuid "d93ff637-1a41-5c2a-a409-3b1e7bff5ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "b=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548778} {:answer/id #uuid "e0d1f152-2d71-5a47-a7da-fd041217b7f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a\\ne 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548789}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548524} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5178042-2ee2-5608-860d-fde87cfb2607" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164433} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa9f4f97-14d1-55b4-9c75-c0369f27d217" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "counterclockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164438} {:answer/id #uuid "78ed1003-d99d-5872-97f8